slacker-gui 1.0.0
=================

GTK4/libadwaita front-end for slacker. It contains no package logic: it
runs the slacker binary, reads what slacker prints, and lays it out.

  Doctor         slacker --version, slacker status
  Search         slacker search NAME              (one exact name)
  Updates        slacker check-updates
                 update / install-new / upgrade-all        (root)
  Installed      slacker history --installed
                 reinstall / remove                        (root)
  Repositories   slacker list-repos
  Mirrors        slacker find-mirror            (on request; read-only:
                                                the mirror is changed by
                                                hand, from a terminal)
  Frozen & Pins  slacker frozen, slacker pin      (root: slacker lists
                                                these only to root; read
                                                on request)
                 add:    frozen RULE, pin REPO:PKG          (root)
                 remove: unfrozen RULE, unpin PKG           (root)
  History        slacker history --last 300
  Details        slacker info NAME

  read-only      slacker <cmd>                  as the desktop user
  changes        pkexec slacker <cmd>           as root; slacker asks its
                                                own questions and the user
                                                answers them in the window
                                                (unfrozen/unpin ask nothing,
                                                so the GUI asks first)

Requirements
------------
  GTK >= 4.0, libadwaita >= 1.5 (the development branch ships 1.9),
  gtk4-rs 0.10 / libadwaita-rs 0.8, rustc >= 1.83,
  a polkit authentication agent in the session.

Build
-----
  cargo build --release
  cargo test --release      # parsers, against fixtures/

Install
-------
  target/release/slacker-gui          -> /usr/bin/slacker-gui
  data/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerGui.desktop
                                      -> /usr/share/applications/
  data/icons/hicolor/                 -> /usr/share/icons/hicolor/
  data/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.slacker.policy
                                      -> /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/
  data/doinst.sh                      icon and desktop cache refresh

  e.g. in a SlackBuild:
    install -Dm755 target/release/slacker-gui $PKG/usr/bin/slacker-gui
    install -Dm644 data/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerGui.desktop \
      $PKG/usr/share/applications/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerGui.desktop
    install -Dm644 data/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.slacker.policy \
      $PKG/usr/share/polkit-1/actions/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.slacker.policy
    mkdir -p $PKG/usr/share/icons
    cp -a data/icons/hicolor $PKG/usr/share/icons/
    cat data/doinst.sh >> $PKG/install/doinst.sh

Icons: 16, 22, 24, 32, 48, 64, 128, 256, 512 px PNG plus scalable SVG,
all named nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerGui. 16-24 px come from a simplified drawing
(data/icons/source/slacker-gui-small.svg); the rest and the scalable icon
from data/icons/source/slacker-gui.svg. To regenerate:
    for s in 16 22 24; do rsvg-convert -w $s -h $s data/icons/source/slacker-gui-small.svg \
      -o data/icons/hicolor/${s}x${s}/apps/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerGui.png; done
    for s in 32 48 64 128 256 512; do rsvg-convert -w $s -h $s data/icons/source/slacker-gui.svg \
      -o data/icons/hicolor/${s}x${s}/apps/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerGui.png; done
Run uninstalled, the window finds no icon; that is expected.

The polkit policy has one action per install location (auth_admin_keep:
one password for a few minutes): /usr/bin, /usr/sbin, /usr/local/bin and
/usr/local/sbin. For any other path (SLACKER_BIN) pkexec falls back to
its generic action, which asks for the password every time.

Finding slacker
---------------
/usr/bin, /usr/sbin, /usr/local/bin, /usr/local/sbin, in that order; the
Overview page warns when more than one exists (a leftover binary). SLACKER_BIN=/absolute/path overrides the search.

Output
------
Commands run one at a time, with LC_ALL=C, TERM=dumb and NO_COLOR=1.
Read-only commands get stdin closed. stderr is merged into stdout. Every command and its full
output is in the Command Output dialog: main menu (F10), or
Ctrl+Shift+O.

Questions
---------
No command gets --yes. A change runs in a window with its live output,
and stdin stays open to slacker. When slacker stops on one of its own
questions the window shows it with buttons, and the answer is written
to slacker's stdin exactly as it would be typed on a terminal:
  ... [y/N]                    Yes / No (Enter = slacker's default)
  Choice [c/r/a]: + [x]word    one row per option; "(default)" marked
  Enter numbers to VERB ...    package checklist -> Enter / "1 3" / n
  N repo(s) to update ...      repository checklist -> a / "1 2" / n
The answer is echoed onto the question line in the output. The
recognised shapes follow slacker's source (src/parse/prompt.rs); if
output stops for a few seconds on a line that is none of them, the
window offers "Stop Answering", which closes stdin: slacker then reads
end-of-file, and its default for every change is no.
Freeze and pin are also in the menu of every row on the Installed page.
Reinstall is offered only for packages a configured repository serves:
history labels each package with that repository, or with its build tag
(e.g. SBo) when no repository does, and list-repos gives the names.

Once the pins have been read, Search and Installed mark pinned packages.
Frozen rules are shown as slacker lists them; the GUI does not match
them against packages itself (rules are globs, regexes and series).

Parsers follow the println! formats in slacker's source. A line they do
not recognise is shown as printed, never guessed at.
Exit codes 20 (nothing found), 50 (slacker upgraded itself) and
100 (updates pending) are answers, not failures.
